# THE STYLESHEET IS DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED.
#
# It selects on escaped Tailwind classes containing CSS hex escapes, e.g.
#   .shadow-\[0_1px_0_hsl\(var\(--foreground\)\/0\.08\)\2c 0_2px_0_hsl\(…\)\]
# A hex escape (`\2c`) is terminated by exactly ONE whitespace character, so
# that trailing space is part of the token, not formatting. Prettier wraps the
# line there and consumes the space as a newline, which turns a single class
# selector into a descendant combinator — the rule then silently matches
# nothing. Verified: running prettier on this file breaks the tabs section and
# check-exact-classes.py catches it.
#
# The file is hand-formatted and machine-checked instead:
#   node tools/check-css.js  — brace/paren/comment balance, indentation,
#                              declarations outside blocks, untagged !important
